WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.522
Elmi Guray Academy.

2
00:00:02.472 --> 00:00:04.470
Lesson 4.

3
00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:08.125
AI Tool Costs and Changing Results.

4
00:00:08.284 --> 00:00:16.685
Technical Explanation — English AI development tools can improve productivity, but many of them are not completely free.

5
00:00:16.635 --> 00:00:32.599
Some services may offer: A free trial A limited free plan A small number of monthly requests Access to fewer AI models Reduced speed or fewer features These free options may be useful for learning, experimenting, or testing a tool.

6
00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:37.939
However, regular professional use may require a paid subscription.

7
00:00:37.939 --> 00:00:44.298
Why AI Tools Cost Money AI systems require powerful computer infrastructure.

8
00:00:44.298 --> 00:00:50.167
When a developer sends a prompt, the service may need to: Receive the request.

9
00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:52.355
Process the prompt.

10
00:00:52.355 --> 00:00:55.126
Read project context.

11
00:00:55.126 --> 00:00:57.491
Run an AI model.

12
00:00:57.491 --> 00:00:59.855
Generate a response.

13
00:00:59.855 --> 00:01:02.762
Send the result back to the user.

14
00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:11.078
This process uses servers, electricity, networking, storage, security systems, and technical support.

15
00:01:11.078 --> 00:01:18.061
Therefore, service providers often charge users when usage becomes frequent or advanced.

16
00:01:18.061 --> 00:01:45.289
Free Plans and Paid Plans Plan Type Possible Benefits Possible Limitations Free plan Useful for testing and basic learning Limited prompts, features, speed, or models Paid plan Higher limits, more features, and more reliable access Monthly or yearly cost Team plan Shared administration, controls, and team features Higher cost and account-management needs The exact plans may differ between providers.

17
00:01:45.289 --> 00:01:52.694
Students should always read the current pricing, limitations, and cancellation rules before subscribing.

18
00:01:52.694 --> 00:01:59.569
Budgeting for AI Tools Developers should treat AI subscriptions like other professional tools.

19
00:01:59.569 --> 00:02:03.822
Before paying, ask: Do I use this tool regularly?

20
00:02:03.822 --> 00:02:06.472
Does it save meaningful time?

21
00:02:06.472 --> 00:02:09.325
Does it improve my work quality?

22
00:02:09.325 --> 00:02:12.708
Can one tool replace another subscription?

23
00:02:12.708 --> 00:02:15.493
Is the monthly cost affordable?

24
00:02:15.493 --> 00:02:17.857
Can I cancel easily?

25
00:02:17.857 --> 00:02:21.105
Does the plan include the features I need?

26
00:02:21.105 --> 00:02:27.151
EGA Budget Principle Do not pay for an AI tool only because it is popular.

27
00:02:27.151 --> 00:02:31.689
Pay when it gives clear value to your learning or development work.

28
00:02:31.689 --> 00:02:40.113
AI Results Are Not Always Identical AI tools may produce different answers even when two users enter similar prompts.

29
00:02:40.113 --> 00:03:00.357
Results may change because of: Different wording in the prompt Different project files Different account settings Different AI models Changes made by the service provider Different conversation history Different software versions Therefore, students should not expect every generated answer to match a course demonstration exactly.

30
00:03:00.357 --> 00:03:06.295
AI Models Change Over Time AI providers regularly update their systems.

31
00:03:06.295 --> 00:03:26.920
A newer model may: Understand instructions better Generate different code Use a different writing style Support longer project context Include new features Remove or rename older features The interface of GitHub Copilot, Cursor, ChatGPT, or another AI service may also change after a lesson is created.

32
00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:34.379
Students should focus on the method and principles, rather than memorizing one exact screen or response.

33
00:03:34.379 --> 00:03:42.871
Focus on the Workflow, Not the Exact Output The main purpose of an AI-development lesson is to teach a repeatable workflow.

34
00:03:42.871 --> 00:03:47.260
A useful workflow is: Understand the development task.

35
00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:50.072
Choose the correct AI tool.

36
00:03:50.072 --> 00:03:52.368
Write a clear prompt.

37
00:03:52.368 --> 00:03:54.963
Add useful context.

38
00:03:54.963 --> 00:03:57.694
Review the generated result.

39
00:03:57.694 --> 00:03:59.637
Test the code.

40
00:03:59.637 --> 00:04:01.716
Correct errors.

41
00:04:01.716 --> 00:04:04.569
Save the verified solution.

42
00:04:04.569 --> 00:04:11.526
Even when the AI produces a different response, the same review and testing process still applies.

43
00:04:11.526 --> 00:04:19.991
Example: Different Results from Similar Prompts Consider these two prompts: Create an HTML registration form.

44
00:04:19.991 --> 00:04:31.010
Create a beginner-friendly HTML student-registration form with name, email, phone, course selection, labels, required fields, and a submit button.

45
00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:34.393
The second prompt contains more detail.

46
00:04:34.393 --> 00:04:40.588
It is likely to produce a more specific result because the AI has clearer requirements.

47
00:04:40.588 --> 00:04:45.031
This shows that prompt quality can affect output quality.

48
00:04:45.031 --> 00:04:52.925
Never Depend on One Generated Result A developer should not assume that the first AI response is the final answer.

49
00:04:52.925 --> 00:05:08.510
A better approach is to: Read the response carefully Ask follow-up questions Request corrections Compare possible solutions Test the code Keep a working backup AI assistance is an interactive process, not a guarantee of perfect output.

50
00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:12.463
Safe Subscription Practices Confirm the official

51
00:05:12.628 --> 00:05:15.064
provider before paying.

52
00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:18.574
Read whether the price is monthly or yearly.

53
00:05:18.574 --> 00:05:21.332
Check whether taxes are added.

54
00:05:21.332 --> 00:05:24.253
Understand automatic renewal.

55
00:05:24.253 --> 00:05:26.807
Save payment receipts.

56
00:05:26.807 --> 00:05:29.280
Use a strong password.

57
00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:33.193
Enable two-factor authentication when available.

58
00:05:33.193 --> 00:05:36.074
Cancel unused subscriptions.

59
00:05:36.074 --> 00:05:39.606
Never share an account password with students.

60
00:05:39.606 --> 00:05:48.003
HTML Learning in This Lesson This lesson uses HTML to teach both AI concepts and webpage structure.

61
00:05:48.003 --> 00:06:04.416
Important HTML features in this lesson include: The <meta> element The name attribute The content attribute The <article> element The <blockquote> element Table elements The Meta Description Element A meta description provides a short description of a webpage.

62
00:06:04.416 --> 00:06:12.799
HTML Code <meta name="description" content="A lesson about AI tool costs and changing results.

63
00:06:12.799 --> 00:06:16.345
The <meta> element is placed inside the <head> .

64
00:06:16.345 --> 00:06:19.158
It does not use a closing tag.

65
00:06:19.158 --> 00:06:23.737
name="description" identifies the type of metadata.

66
00:06:23.737 --> 00:06:27.364
content contains the webpage description.

67
00:06:27.364 --> 00:06:32.989
The meta description does not normally appear inside the visible webpage body.

68
00:06:32.989 --> 00:06:38.193
The Head and Body Difference The <head> contains information about the webpage.

69
00:06:38.193 --> 00:06:42.473
The <body> contains content that users see in the browser.

70
00:06:42.473 --> 00:06:57.269
head> <title> Lesson 4 </title> <meta name="description" content="Lesson description" > </head> <body> <h1> Visible Lesson Title </h1> </body> Browser Output The title may appear in the browser tab.

71
00:06:57.269 --> 00:07:01.087
The heading appears inside the visible webpage.

72
00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:05.802
The Table Element Reminder The plan comparison uses a table.

73
00:07:05.802 --> 00:07:39.742
table border="1"> <tr> <th>Plan</th> <th>Limit</th> </tr> <tr> <td>Free</td> <td>Limited usage</td> </tr> </table> Browser Output Plan Limit Free Limited usage Image Path Reminder The EGA logo uses: <img src="images/ega-logo.png" alt="Elmi Guray Academy logo" width="180" > The image works because ega-logo.png is stored inside the images folder.

74
00:07:39.742 --> 00:07:43.913
Important Rules Free access may have usage limits.

75
00:07:43.913 --> 00:07:47.894
Regular professional use may require payment.

76
00:07:47.894 --> 00:07:51.291
Check current pricing before subscribing.

77
00:07:51.291 --> 00:07:54.593
Do not pay for tools you do not use.

78
00:07:54.593 --> 00:07:58.180
AI results may differ between users.

79
00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:01.794
AI models and interfaces may change.

80
00:08:01.794 --> 00:08:05.938
Focus on the workflow, not one exact response.

81
00:08:05.938 --> 00:08:09.321
Review and test all generated code.

82
00:08:09.321 --> 00:08:13.261
Save receipts and monitor recurring subscriptions.

83
00:08:13.261 --> 00:08:16.998
Never share passwords or payment details.

84
00:08:16.998 --> 00:08:43.112
Common Beginner Mistakes Assuming every AI tool is permanently free Forgetting about automatic renewal Paying before testing the free plan Expecting exactly the same AI answer as another user Copying an AI response without testing it Believing an old course interface will never change Paying for several overlapping tools Ignoring monthly subscription costs Using the wrong image path in HTML

